.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-journal-2026-07-01
.Nd working notes of 2026-07-01
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss Switch prose font hook from variable-pitch-mode to mixed-pitch-mode (keep Org tables and code aligned)
.Ss Summary
.Ql "init-writing.el"
applied
.Ql "(text-mode . variable-pitch-mode)"
to every
.Ql "text-mode" Ns No "-derived"
buffer.
.Ql "variable-pitch-mode"
makes the \fIwhole\fP buffer proportional, so Org (which aligns tables by padding cells with spaces) rendered ragged tables: a monospace-only trick applied under a proportional font.
The same hit source blocks and verbatim spans.
.Pp
Swapped in the
.Ql "mixed-pitch"
package (MELPA, jabranham).
.Ql "mixed-pitch-mode"
remaps the buffer default to
.Ql "variable-pitch"
for prose while keeping a curated face list
.No \&( Ns Ql "mixed-pitch-fixed-pitch-faces"
—
.Ql "org-table" ,
.Ql "org-code" ,
.Ql "org-block" ,
.Ql "org-verbatim" ,
.Ql "org-formula" ,
…) pinned to
.Ql "fixed-pitch" .
Org tables align again; prose stays proportional.
It reuses the same
.Ql "variable-pitch"
face that
.Ql "init-ui.el"
already configures, so no font/theme change was needed.
.Pp
Two follow-on decisions:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fBCommit-message and email buffers are now fully monospaced.\fP They derive from
.Ql "text-mode"
and were proportional before; they are column-sensitive (50/72 rule), so a new opt-out turns
.Ql "mixed-pitch-mode"
back off there.
.It
\fBMarkdown uses the
.Ql "mixed-pitch"
default face list\fP (no extra faces added); Org is the case that mattered and is covered out of the box.
.El
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "lisp/init-writing.el" Ns No "\fP"
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Dropped
.Ql "(text-mode . variable-pitch-mode)"
from the
.Ql "text-mode"
.Ql "use-package"
.Ql ":hook"
(kept
.Ql "visual-line-mode" ,
.Ql "visual-wrap-prefix-mode" )
and reworded its
.Ql ";;; @doc" .
.It
Added a
.Ql "use-package mixed-pitch"
block.
.Ql ":hook"
enables
.Ql "mixed-pitch-mode"
in
.Ql "text-mode" ,
and a
.Ql ":preface"
helper
.Ql "jotain-writing--keep-monospace"
(calls
.Ql "(mixed-pitch-mode -1)" )
is hooked to
.Ql "git-commit-setup"
and
.Ql "message-mode"
for the monospace opt-out.
.Ql "git-commit-setup-hook"
and
.Ql "message-mode-hook"
both run after
.Ql "text-mode-hook" ,
so the opt-out cleanly reverses it.
Added
.Ql "(declare-function mixed-pitch-mode \(dqmixed-pitch\(dq …)" .
.It
The helper lives in
.Ql ":preface"
(not between the
.Ql ";;; @doc"
and the
.Ql "use-package"
form) so
.Ql "nix/packages-doc.nix"
still associates the doc block with the block — otherwise the generated reference showed
.Ql "_Undocumented._" .
.El
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "lisp/init-lang-data.el" Ns No "\fP"
— in
.Ql "jotain-lang-data--enable-prog-mode-features"
(the YAML prose-off workaround), changed
.Ql "(variable-pitch-mode -1)"
to
.Ql "(mixed-pitch-mode -1)"
and added the matching
.Ql "declare-function" ;
without this YAML buffers would keep a proportional font.
Updated the docstring wording.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "bench/find-file-bench.el" Ns No "\fP"
— updated the timed-minor-modes list
.No \&( Ns Ql "variable-pitch-mode"
→
.Ql "mixed-pitch-mode" )
so the find-file benchmark measures the mode that now fires in
.Ql "text-mode" .
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "docs/configuration/package-reference.mdx" Ns No "\fP"
— regenerated via
.Ql "just docs-refresh-packages"
from the updated
.Ql ";;; @doc"
blocks (adds a
.Ql "### mixed-pitch"
section, reworks
.Ql "### text-mode" ).
Not hand-edited; CI's
.Ql "packages-doc-in-sync"
check verifies the in-tree copy.
.El
.Pp
Nix build needed no manual package entry:
.Ql "nix/use-package.nix"
auto-scans the new
.Ql "(use-package mixed-pitch …)"
and resolves it to
.Ql "epkgs.mixed-pitch" .
.Ss Verification
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ql "just docs-refresh-packages"
— regenerated cleanly;
.Ql "### mixed-pitch"
section present, no
.Ql "_Undocumented._" .
.It
.Ql "just check"
— flake check (byte-compile with warnings-as-errors, paren check, statix/deadnix/nixfmt,
.Ql "packages-doc-in-sync" ).
.It
Manual
.No \&( Ns Ql "just run-built" ):
Org numeric table aligns and right-justifies; YAML stays monospaced; Markdown prose is proportional; magit commit buffer is monospaced.
.El
.Ss Compatibility note
Only
.Ql "text-mode" Ns No "-derived"
buffers change.
Code modes were never hooked;
.Ql "conf-mode"
is not
.Ql "text-mode" Ns No "-derived."
.Ql "denote"
notes and Markdown prose stay proportional (now with monospaced code spans).
.Ql "init-ui.el"
faces and
.Ql "init-org.el" Ns No "/org-modern"
are unchanged.
.Ss Incidental: byte-compile fix in init-snippets.el
The first
.Ql "just check"
after the edits failed on
.Ql "lisp/init-snippets.el:51"
—
.Ql "make-variable-buffer-local' not called at toplevel" .
That file is untouched by this change; editing
.Ql "lisp/"
merely busted the cached
.Ql "elisp-compile"
result from before the last nix-inputs bump, so the newer byte-compiler's stricter warning (now an error under
.Ql "byte-compile-error-on-warn" )
surfaced on the forced rebuild.
The
.Ql "defvar-local"
guard for the merged tempel+eglot capf lived inside
.Ql "use-package tempel" Ns No "'s"
.Ql ":init" ,
where it is not a toplevel form.
Hoisted it to true top level;
.Ql "just check"
is green (all 8 flake checks pass).
